## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical experience with SAP on AWS and governance services, introducing a new angle: license compliance using native AWS tooling.

## Key Concepts

- AWS License Manager
- SSM Run Command
- CloudWatch, S3, and SNS integration
- Entitlements drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: minimal Lambda to fetch License Manager data (pseudo)
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const lm = new AWS.LicenseManager();
exports.handler = async () => {
  const conf = await lm.listLicenseConfigurations({ /* params */ }).promise();
  // fetch SAP license data from SAP host and compare to entitlements
  return conf;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this for multiple SAP instances across regions?
- What limitations exist for SAP licensing with License Manager in EC2?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region SAP auth models, data residency, and auditable ops in a real-world multi-account setup.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region SAP HANA access control with IAM/SCP mappings
- Just-In-Time (JIT) operator elevation with MFA
- PrivateLink for SAP component isolation across regions
- Centralized logging and compliance (CloudTrail, CloudWatch, Config)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Resources": {
    "SAPCrossAccountRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [
            {
              "Effect": "Allow",
              "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::[OPERATIONS_ACCOUNT]:root"},
              "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
              "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"}}
            }
          ]
        },
        "PermissionsBoundary": {"Fn::Join": ["", ["arn:aws:iam::", {"Ref": "AWS::AccountId"}, ":policy/SAPOperatorBoundary"]]},
        "Policies": [{
          "PolicyName": "SAPOperatorPolicy",
          "PolicyDocument": {
            "Version": "2012-10-17",
            "Statement": [{"Effect": "Allow", "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"], "Resource": "*"}]
          }
        }]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify and rotate SAP authorizations when roles drift?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect unauthorized JIT elevations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces hands-on observability basics for SAP on AWS, covering log shipping, custom metrics, and alerting.

## Key Concepts
- CloudWatch Logs and CloudWatch Agent for centralized log management
- PutMetricData API for publishing custom metrics like SAP_CPU_GT_85
- CloudWatch Alarms for threshold-based alerting
- SNS for reliable notification delivery
- CloudFormation for Infrastructure as Code (IAM role and alarm creation)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Resources": {
    "SAPCloudWatchLogsRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [{
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": {"Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com"},
            "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
          }]
        },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": ["arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy"]
      }
    },
    "SAPCPUAlarm": {
      "Type": "AWS::CloudWatch::Alarm",
      "Properties": {
        "AlarmName": "SAP_CPU_GT_85",
        "MetricName": "SAP_CPU_GT_85",
        "Namespace": "SAP/Application",
        "Statistic": "Maximum",
        "Period": 300,
        "EvaluationPeriods": 1,
        "Threshold": 85,
        "ComparisonOperator": "GreaterThanThreshold",
        "AlarmActions": [{"Ref": "SAPSNSTopic"}],
        "TreatMissingData": "notBreaching"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests designing a production-grade DR workflow for SAP HANA on AWS, balancing RPO/RTO while maintaining security and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- SAP HANA System Replication (SDR) across regions
- EventBridge, Step Functions orchestration, Route 53 failover
- Cross-account IAM roles, SCPs, and KMS-encrypted backups
- Testing plans and validation of failover
- Observability of replication lag and failover success

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: trigger DR failover via Step Functions
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const sfn = new AWS.StepFunctions();
async function triggerFailover(stateMachineArn, input){
  const params = { stateMachineArn, input: JSON.stringify(input) };
  return sfn.startExecution(params).promise();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test RPO/RTO regularly without impacting production?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect failing SDR synchronization?
